'' The source lock over arrays (docs/tiko-slices RFC-0003 §7, TKO1062): REDIM PRESERVE, ERASE
'' and passing the array to an 'x()' parameter (which may REDIM it) while a span of a dynamic
'' array is still to be used. A fixed array is never locked; a span rebound after the REDIM is
'' fine; and a STRING slice of an element of a dynamic string array is locked by REDIM too.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/array-slice-lock.tiko
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: array-slice-lock.tiko(8,1): error TKO1062: 'd' cannot be changed while slice 'v' borrows from it (last used at line 9)
'' EXPECT-OUT: array-slice-lock.tiko(11,1): error TKO1062: 'd' cannot be changed while slice 'w' borrows from it (last used at line 12)
'' EXPECT-OUT: array-slice-lock.tiko(15,5): error TKO1062: 'd' cannot be changed while slice 'x' borrows from it (last used at line 16)
'' EXPECT-OUT: array-slice-lock.tiko(31,1): error TKO1062: 'q' cannot be changed while slice 'ql' borrows from it (last used at line 32)
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 4
